# Sovereign UI SDK Governance

Read `user_uploads/ai_os_tailwind_shadcn_component_spec.md` before building or reviewing UI.

## Architecture

- `client/src/ui-core/` = Sovereign wrapper layer (the ONLY approved import path for agents)
- `client/src/components/ui/` = raw shadcn primitives (discovery only, never import in feature code)
- `client/src/ui-core/tokens/` = design tokens (spacing, radius, shadow, color, typography, motion)

## Non-negotiable rules

1. Agents import from `@/ui-core` only — never `@/components/ui/*` in feature pages
2. No inline `style={{}}` for spacing, color, radius, shadow, or layout
3. No arbitrary hex values in feature files — use tokens or Tailwind theme
4. No duplicate component systems (no raw MUI, no ad hoc Tailwind blocks)
5. L0-L1 surfaces (identity shell, footer, system menu) are protected from agent mutation
6. All interactive cards require `motion` from `framer-motion`
7. Primary containers use `rounded-2xl` (24px)
8. Touch targets minimum 44x44 (WCAG AAA)
9. One font family: Inter
10. Brand green used sparingly — semantic colors for meaning only

## Component roles

Every component must support one of: control, display, inspection, input, feedback, overlay

## Spacing

8-point base. Component padding: p-4 to p-6. Section spacing: gap-6 to gap-8.

## Shadows

- Cards: shadow-os-md
- Overlays: shadow-os-lg
- Active PTT: shadow-os-glow

## Promotion workflow

1. Discover via shadcn MCP
2. Evaluate against existing Sovereign wrappers
3. If missing, promote into ui-core with tokens and variants
4. Document usage before broad adoption
